::kind(api)

::meta{crate: tomet-lsp, dependencies: list(cotomet, cotomet-eval, tomet-address, tomet-ast, tomet-cst, tomet-declaration, tomet-expr, tomet-formatter, tomet-lexer, tomet-load, tomet-load-config, tomet-parser, tomet-semantics, tomet-tree, tomet-validator), dependents: list()}

=[tomet-lsp]

Language server library for Tomet (`tomet-lsp`).
Provides diagnostics (what the text alone says, and what `tomet check`
says of a document in its vault), document formatting, hover, document
symbols, goto definition, and completions. A standalone cotomet file
(`.ctmt`) is served as data: see [`data`].

==[Module completion]

===[Functions]

====[fn completions_for]

Provides autocompletion items for elements, keywords, and builtin compute functions.

====[fn completions_for_with_uri]

Provides autocompletion items with document URI awareness for path completions.

==[Module data]

A standalone cotomet file (`.ctmt`) as the language server serves it.

It is data, not a document: the cotomet parser says what is wrong with it,
the whitespace formatter formats it, and the features that read a document
(hover, symbols, completion, folding, definition) have nothing to say. It
never reaches the vault, which holds documents.

===[Functions]

====[fn is_data_uri]

Whether `uri` names a `.ctmt` file. The query and fragment are not part of
the name.

====[fn request_is_for_data]

Whether a request's `params` are about a `.ctmt`: the document a request
names is at `textDocument.uri` in all of them.

====[fn data_diagnostics_for]

What the cotomet parser and evaluator say of `text` as a standalone file.

Returns parse errors, declaration errors, and expression evaluation errors,
underlined at their locations in the source text.

==[Module definition]

===[Functions]

====[fn definition_for]

Provides Goto Definition target for reference links or interpolation
expressions, from the text alone: the references to a node of the same
document. One into another document needs the vault
([`Workspace::definition`](crate::Workspace::definition)).

==[Module diagnostic]

===[Functions]

====[fn diagnostics_for]

Parses `text` and produces diagnostics (both parse errors and CST validation rules).

==[Module folding]

Provides folding ranges for sections, blocks, and comments in the editor.

===[Functions]

====[fn folding_ranges_for]

Computes folding ranges for the given document text.

==[Module format]

===[Functions]

====[fn format_edits]

Formats the document using `tomet-formatter` with loaded or inferred configuration.

A `.ctmt` is formatted by whitespace alone, whatever the config says, as
`tomet format` does.

====[fn resolve_effective_config]

Resolves the merged configuration for a document by combining:
1. Workspace config discovered from ancestor directories (`default.config.tmt` / `tomet.config.tmt`)
2. Explicit `::config(import: ...)` / `::config(file: ...)` imported configs
3. Document's local `::config` definitions (highest precedence)

==[Module hover]

===[Functions]

====[fn hover_for]

Provides hover information for the symbol under the cursor, from the text
alone.

An expression is evaluated against this one document and its settings, so
what reaches for another file fails and says so. A document that has a
vault is better served by [`hover_in`], with the vault's evaluation.

====[fn hover_in]

[`hover_for`], with `evaluate` deciding what an expression comes to.

===[Type Aliases]

====[type Evaluate]

What an expression comes to, for a hover: given the document it is written
in, and the expression.

==[Module position]

===[Structs]

====[struct TextPositions]

Converts between byte offsets into one document's text and LSP positions
(a 0-based line and a UTF-16 character offset within it).

Spans and parse errors carry byte offsets only. Build one of these per
request, from the text the request is about, and pass it down: building it
is one pass over the text, and every conversion after that is cheap.

===[Functions]

====[fn uri_to_file_path]

==[Module symbol]

===[Functions]

====[fn document_symbols_for]

Provides document symbols for outline navigation in the editor.

==[Module workspace]

The vaults the open documents belong to, and the diagnostics that need one.

[`diagnostics_for`](crate::diagnostics_for) reads a document from its text
alone: what the parser and the CST validator can say. What `tomet check`
says needs more -- the vocabularies in scope, the blueprint the `::kind`
names, the settings' field types, the files an `include` reads -- and all
of that belongs to a vault. [`Workspace`] finds the vault of each open
document the way the CLI does, from the file's own path, and asks it for
the same findings `tomet check` reports.

===[Structs]

====[struct Workspace]

The open documents, and the vaults they are in.

====[struct Debounce]

Waits until things have stopped changing: each [`touch`](Debounce::touch)
pushes the moment back, and [`due`](Debounce::due) says when it has come.

What a vault is asked for on every keystroke would be wasted work for a
document being typed into, so it is done once the typing pauses.

===[Functions]

====[fn to_diagnostics]

`findings` of the document with text `text`, as LSP diagnostics.

The validator's duplicate-id finding is left out: the CST validator
reports the same thing from `diagnostics_for`, on the exact tokens.
